<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output down 0.7% yr/yr in April. [CORRECTED 15:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output down 0.7% yr/yr in April. [CORRECTED 15:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	   April 97    March 97	April 96</p>
<p>						   (corrects month)</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   101.0     109.6	    101.7</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and</p>
<p>composition of the months</p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) April 97   March 97	April 96</p>
<p>						     (corrects month)</p>
<p> industry as a whole		 96.9	 96.9	     93.7</p>
<p> construction industry	     81.8	 81.5	     71.7</p>
<p> investment goods		    97.5	 98.1	     97.6</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
